-- Department of Posts (Ministry of Communications). Deepened 2026-09-04
-- (depth pass — see docs/DEPTH_PASS_PLAN.md) beyond the original bounded
-- pass (one 4-node chain). Distinct from the Department of
-- Telecommunications side of this ministry (db/seed_communications.sql).
-- Generated from the research log by a one-off script (scratchpad
-- gen_posts.py); 32 of the 38 tracked Posts notifications were read from
-- the official egazette.gov.in PDF ('primary-source-full-text'), the rest
-- from the aggregator's Full Text.
--
-- The Post Office Regulations, 2024 chain is not 4 nodes but 15:
-- principal + 14 amendments (seven in 2025, seven in 2026), every one
-- carrying a trailing Note naming the principal and the immediately
-- preceding amendment. The previously-modeled S.O. 4053(E) is the FIFTH
-- Amendment of 2026 and is now re-parented onto the Fourth (S.O.
-- 3891(E)) rather than the principal. S.O. 4537(E) is the Seventh
-- Amendment 2026; nothing later exists (listing checked to 2026-09-03).
--
-- REAL CITING-TEXT ERRORS kept as observed: the Second Amendment 2025
-- is G.S.R. 263(E) by its own official text (the only G.S.R.-numbered
-- link in an S.O. chain), but the Third Amendment's Note cites it as
-- "S.O. 263 (E)" — modeled to the document's own identity. The Indian
-- Post Office (2nd Amendment) Rules, 2023 is dated 22 May 2023 in its
-- own text; the 3rd Amendment cites it as "23rd May" (its gazette
-- publication date). G.S.R. 767(E) twice prints "suppression" for
-- "supersession".
--
-- The Indian Post Office Rules, 1933 chain: G.S.R. 17(E) [2023-01-10]
-- carries a 207-entry enumerated amendment history (1975-2022) in its
-- own Note, transcribed in full and modeled as a linear chain with
-- position-encoded gazette_ids (dop-ipo-NNN-YYYY) because the list
-- reuses numbers freely (462(E) 1988 vs 2023; 639(E) 1988 vs 2023;
-- 379(E) three times; 43(E) as both G.S.R. and S.O. on the same day, and
-- more). Two honest gaps: entry 199 is the Finance Act, 2017 (an Act,
-- not a notification) — no edge bridges 198->200; entry 78 (GSR 967)
-- gives only "December, 1989" — 1989-12-01 is a placeholder day. The
-- 1933 principal is cited only as "Posts and Telegraphs Manual Volume-I,
-- Fifth Edition" (no number) and the 2024 Post Office Rules supersede
-- the 1933 Rules as an instrument, also numberless — both deferred.
--
-- 6 further threads: Postal Assistant/Sorting Assistant, Multi Tasking
-- Staff, and Postman/Mail Guard Recruitment Rules note-chains; an RPLI
-- bonus corrigendum (Hindi-only, file-number-identified, Part I); a PLI/
-- RPLI governance notification citing S.O. 5440(E) by number; and two
-- 2025 PLI-fund notifications modifying one 2016 file-number-identified
-- notification (bare).
--
-- Cross-ministry number collisions with existing seeds, all kept distinct
-- by ministry-prefixed gazette_id: S.O. 659(E) (2026 vs Chemicals 2025),
-- S.O. 4375(E) (2025 vs Jal Shakti 2023), G.S.R. 382(E) (2023 vs Mines
-- 2025), G.S.R. 459(E) (2022 vs I&B 1996/2006), G.S.R. 781(E) (2018 vs
-- Petroleum 2013/2026), G.S.R. 21(E) (2023 vs DoPT 2026), G.S.R. 157(E)
-- (2020 vs Power 2026), G.S.R. 294(E) (deferred, vs Mines 2022).
--
-- egazette URL hazard found: S.O. 6154(E) (notified 31 Dec 2025,
-- published 1 Jan 2026) is served from /WriteReadData/2025/, not /2026/
-- — ingest/egazette.py should fall back to year-1 and verify a %PDF body.
--
-- Real leads NOT modeled: G.S.R. 294(E) (JTO Recruitment Rules, 2026)
-- supersedes the 1996 JHT/SHT Rules by title only; Post Office Life
-- Insurance Rules, 2011 cited by gazette issue number only; six PLI/RPLI
-- bonus declarations that stand alone; two commencement notifications
-- citing Acts, not notifications.


